+## 2026-11-01: warning for truncated search terms in query filters (#44464)
+
+`Redmine::Search::Tokenizer` now has `MAX_TOKENS = 5` and `truncated?`. `Query#filter_warnings` returns one message per string, text or search filter whose value has more than 5 terms with a tokenizing operator (`~`, `*~`, `!~`, `^`, `$`). `QueriesHelper#query_filter_warnings` renders them as `p.warning` in `queries/_query_form` (issues, time entries, projects, users), the calendar and the Gantt chart. The query stays valid and results are shown. Tests in search_test, query_test and the issues, calendars and gantts functional tests. `bin/harness check` passes (6071 tests, 0 failures). Learned: `bin/rails` uses the Ruby on PATH (macOS 2.6), so prefix PATH with `/opt/homebrew/opt/ruby/bin` and its gem bindir to run single tests. Left: the warning text is only in `en.yml`; other locales fall back to English.
